Package: admiralagent
Title: Spec-Driven ADaM Code Generation with LLM-Translated Layers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jaime", "Yan", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yanmingyunmt@gmail.com")
Description: Translates P21-style ADaM specifications into executable
    'admiral' code with validation comments. An LLM (optional, via
    'ellmer') maps each spec variable's free-text derivation onto a
    closed vocabulary of derivation layers (structured JSON IR); a
    deterministic compiler renders the IR into 'admiral'/'metatools'
    code with 'CHECK' validation comments and writes provenance
    sidecars. Ships with a zero-dependency rule-based classifier as
    baseline and fallback; the LLM never writes R code directly and all
    model output is validated against the closed vocabulary before use.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/yanmingyu92/admiralagent
BugReports: https://github.com/yanmingyu92/admiralagent/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: glue, jsonlite, digest, stats, utils
